*.sln
*.sw?

# Environment. Real values live in .env.local; only the example is committed.
# (*.local above already covers .env.local — this says so on purpose, so the
# glob can change without a project's keys following it into a commit.)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Test coverage
coverage

# Claude Code's launch configuration. It was tracked once, with a single entry
# for this project's own dev server, and then it filled up with entries for
# whatever else happened to be open on the machine -- each one a full path
# through a home directory. This repository is public, so it is kept out of it.
# Nothing is lost: Claude Code writes the file again the first time it needs
# one, and the entry it needs is three lines.
.claude/launch.json

# Brand work that lives beside the project rather than in it: logo candidates,
# colour sets, a guidelines PDF. Several megabytes of workings that no build
# reads, and that would otherwise sit in `git status` forever waiting to be
# swept into a commit by a stray `git add -A`.
brand-kit/
brandkit/
